{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"verdict\": \"cannot_tell\",\n  \"quotes\": [\n    \"We studied subthalamic correlates of turning motions in 13 PwPD (six female, age at onset: 53.1 ± 10.5 years; disease duration 12.6 ± 5.3 years) who had previously undergone bilateral STN-DBS therapy under regular clinical care\",\n    \"Here, we report findings from turning motions with and without FoG in PwPD, in whom we previously reported neuronal abnormalities related to FoG occurring during regular walking.\",\n    \"Klocke, P. et al. Supraspinal contributions to defective antagonistic inhibition and freezing of gait in Parkinson's disease. Brain 147, 4056-4071, doi:10.1093/brain/awae223 (2024).\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"全文能够确认该转弯研究纳入13名患者，也明确说明这些患者此前曾用于报告与常规行走时冻结步态相关的神经异常，引用的是Klocke等人2024年发表于Brain的研究。但这篇论文没有说明该13人转弯研究是否另有正式发表版本，也没有提供预印本与正式论文之间的队列对应关系，更没有涉及报告Y是否同时纳入两个版本。因此，不能仅凭本文确认报告所称的重复纳入及潜在队列重叠，也不能认定指控者指出的具体问题已经得到全文证实。需要特别区分：本文提及的2024年研究是此前关于常规行走时冻结步态的研究，并非文中明确指出的这项转弯研究的正式发表版本。故现有全文不足以判定报告是否误读。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "eadd858b-fbc1-4471-8162-3ae712699248", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261113T104705299378Z", "elapsed_seconds": 26.907, "completed_utc": "2026-11-13T10:47:32.214464+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disabled": true, "temporary_chat_requests_personalization": false, "is_do_not_remember": false, "continuation": false, "unpersonalized_inherited_verified": false, "body_sha256": "590c89839847ca81a56bee909bd73d3edaadcbd7a2b5a7a46e1f63f223f915fb", "attachment_count": 1}, "stream_completion": {"sse_done": true, "message_completed": true, "independent_terminal_verified": true}, "profile": "Nozomi Kasaki / gpt4", "account_sha256": "bbd4fd63